have been referenced in discussions surrounding the evolution and development of mobile banking technologies. HASSA has also played a significant role in addressing terminological differences within the realm of mobile payments. They proposed a comprehensive definition of mobile payments, emphasizing the transfer of funds using a mobile device. Through their work, HASSA has contributed to a clearer understanding of the terminology and processes involved in mobile financial transactions, thereby aiding in the standardization and advancement of mobile banking and payment systems.", "BORCUCH:Borcuch is an author who has been referenced in discussions related to mobile payment technologies. As an individual contributing to this field, Borcuch has provided a definition of mobile payments, describing them as transactions conducted using a mobile device, with the most common device being a mobile phone. This definition highlights the role of mobile devices in facilitating financial transactions, emphasizing the convenience and accessibility they offer in the realm of digital payments. Borcuch's work in this area underscores the growing importance of mobile technology in modern financial systems.", "ZARAŃSKA:Zarańska is an individual who, along with Zborowski, applied a definition of mobile payments as payments made using a mobile device", "ZBOROWSKI:Zborowski is an individual who, along with Zarańska, applied a definition of mobile payments as payments made using a mobile device", "MACIEJEWSKI:Maciejewski is an individual who, along with Polasik, emphasized the complex nature of mobile payments due to the integration of various communication technologies in mobile devices", "GSM:GSM stands for Global System for Mobile Communications, a standard for telecommunication connections used in mobile payments", "NFC:NFC stands for Near Field Communication, a short-range communication technology used in mobile payments", "EBC:", "HCE:HCE, or Host Card Emulation, is a technology that facilitates contactless payments using a mobile phone, functioning similarly to a traditional payment card. This technology enables the virtualization of smart cards through software, allowing users to make mobile payments seamlessly. To utilize HCE, a mobile phone must have internet access, an NFC (Near Field Communication) function, and a compatible bank's mobile application to create and activate a virtual HCE card. Although HCE is a versatile and innovative payment system, its availability is currently limited to only a few banks in Poland. During the pandemic, the use of Host Card Emulation saw significant growth, as it became an integral part of virtual wallets, offering a convenient and secure method for conducting transactions without physical contact.", "APPLE PAY:Apple Pay is a mobile payment and digital wallet service developed by Apple Inc. It allows users to make secure, contactless payments using their Apple devices, such as iPhones, iPads, and Apple Watches. Introduced in Poland in June 2018, Apple Pay has significantly influenced the growth of Host Card Emulation (HCE) cards in the country. The service is available through many banks in Poland and supports transactions in stores, online, and within apps.\n\nApple Pay operates using Near Field Communication (NFC) technology, enabling users to conduct cashless transactions by linking their payment cards, such as Visa or Mastercard, to the app installed on their iOS devices. This system does not store card numbers on the devices or Apple servers, ensuring a high level of security for its users. However, it does not support cash withdrawals from ATMs or peer-to-peer (P2P) transfers.\n\nAs a competitor to BLIK's contactless payment feature, Apple Pay offers a seamless and secure payment experience for users of compatible Apple devices. The service is designed to work with iOS devices, providing a convenient and efficient way to manage digital transactions without the need for physical cards.", "SWATCH PAY:Swatch PAY is a contactless payment system integrated into Swatch watches, enabling users to make payments conveniently with their watches. This innovative technology allows for seamless transactions by simply tapping the watch on a compatible payment terminal, eliminating the need for physical cash or cards. Swatch PAY is designed to offer a secure and efficient payment solution, leveraging the brand's reputation for stylish and functional timepieces. Additionally, Swatch PAY is available in Poland, expanding its reach and providing Polish consumers with a modern and accessible payment option. This integration of payment technology into everyday accessories highlights Swatch's commitment to combining fashion with functionality, catering to the evolving needs of tech-savvy consumers.", "SIKORSKI:Sikorski is an author referenced in the context of mobile payment systems in Poland", "KLIMONTOWICZ:", "MOBILE PAYMENTS:", "GOOGLE WALLET:", "ANDROID PAY:Android Pay is a former name for Google Pay, a mobile payment system for Android devices."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_3a20a5e1b3a8ab617ae81953f3d0cfe063517a525e9803ebb17b90f0421a7fc0_v2"}